// The rabbit, written in Cufet.
//
// ★★ A MODULE THAT OWNS A LIFETIME, and since 2026-09-17 that is what separates a module from a
// book: a book may not own one. This file says `and region` — the claim that pulling it opens a
// lifetime its `Done.` closes — and since 0.25.0 anybody can make the same claim for a type of
// their own. So a rabbit is the first instance of that rule rather than an exception to it; the
// tutorial's last lesson ends here for exactly that reason.
// ⚠ This header used to say a rabbit was "the only thing in the language" that is a region, and
// that letting a person write one was a design mountain. Both stopped being true with `and region`.
//
// A rabbit says so here, in the language, rather than by the
// checker knowing a special name. That is the whole of the definition, and deliberately so:
// a rabbit has no fields (`Pull` has nowhere to put values, as for every module), and its verbs
// are the language's floor rather than methods with Cufet bodies. `bury` suspends the function
// around it, which is a rewrite of that function rather than a call — the same kind of thing
// `If` is, and it is provided by the compiler for the same reason. When the compiler itself is
// written in Cufet, that provision moves with it.
//
// What a rabbit IS, on the other hand, belongs here: an object that says `and region`, pulled
// by name like any module. `Pull a rabbit as hopper.` opens its region, as pulling any region
// does. What still sets the name apart is the parser: `Have rabbit …` addresses the enclosing
// rabbit, which is why the parser still recognises the word.

/// A region you can **bury** work in and **unbury** it from later.
///
/// `Pull a rabbit as hopper.` opens one, and it closes at the matching `Done.` — as any region
/// does. A type of your own becomes one by saying `and region` too.
///
/// ★ Its verbs are the language's floor rather than methods you could have written: `bury`
/// suspends the function around it, which is a REWRITE of that function rather than a call. That
/// is why there is nothing to list here — a rabbit has no members and no fields.
///
/// ⚠ **An address cannot outlive its rabbit.** Anything reaching into the region dies with it, so
/// what you carry out has to be a value rather than a pointer into what was just reclaimed.
Define object rabbit with () and region.
